+            <input id="8fd509e6-ad17-43b5-830a-11d431e48f80" class="off-the-grid" type="radio" name="7199012f-0ff4-445a-85d9-9dfbc06838f4" />
+          <label for="0b540bb4-d467-4fbb-8324-e0d5bee38f6e">Land Records</label>
+          <label for="3709e8b0-4baf-4ae2-9f4c-5c47b16a1074">Recording Information</label>
+          <label for="8fd509e6-ad17-43b5-830a-11d431e48f80">Records Research</label>
+        <div class="tab--container">
+            
+
+
+<div id="" class="tab--block " style="">
+   
+
+
+<p>Our office meticulously maintains and preserves a vast array of land records, including deeds, mortgages, plats, and other pertinent documents essential for property transactions and ownership verification. Whether you're searching for historical deeds or the most recent property transactions, our user-friendly system makes it easy to access the information you need.</p>
+</div>
+
+<div id="" class="tab--block " style="">
+   
+
+
+<p>For individuals or entities involved in property transactions, our office provides a streamlined process for recording deeds, mortgages, and other related documents. Our knowledgeable staff ensures that each document is accurately recorded and securely stored, maintaining the integrity of property ownership records for future generations.</p>
+</div>
+
+<div id="" class="tab--block " style="">
+   
+
+
+<p>Researchers and genealogists will find our office to be a valuable resource for exploring Horry County's rich history through property records. Whether you're tracing the lineage of a family homestead or conducting academic research, our archives offer a wealth of information waiting to be discovered. Our dedicated staff is available to assist with research inquiries and provide guidance on navigating our extensive collection of records.</p>
+</div>
